    {
      "id": "section:7/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "Concurrency-managed workqueues (cmwq)",
      "source_hash": 13401494328781655918,
      "context_hash": 1253950059980085494,
      "translation": "동시성 관리 workqueue(cmwq)",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "workqueue": "workqueue"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:34:23.803649Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:7/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "Since Linux 2.6.36, the kernel uses **concurrency-managed workqueues** (cmwq), introduced by Tejun Heo [(LWN)](https://lwn.net/Articles/394084/).",
      "source_hash": 17837145277659015148,
      "context_hash": 4153576481922500672,
      "translation": "Linux 2.6.36부터 커널은 Tejun Heo가 도입한 **동시성 관리 workqueue**(cmwq)를 사용합니다[(LWN)](https://lwn.net/Articles/394084/).",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "LWN": "LWN",
        "Linux": "Linux",
        "workqueue": "workqueue"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:34:23.803649Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:7/block:1/seg:1",
      "source": "Instead of one thread per CPU, the kernel maintains a pool of workers and dynamically creates/destroys threads based on demand.",
      "source_hash": 17796311606555867949,
      "context_hash": 14990061850631791487,
      "translation": "커널은 CPU마다 스레드 하나를 두는 대신 워커 풀을 유지하며, 수요에 따라 스레드를 동적으로 생성하거나 제거합니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "CPU": "CPU",
        "kernel": "커널",
        "pool": "풀"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:34:23.803649Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:7/block:2/seg:0",
      "source": "The key property: **the kernel tries to keep exactly one runnable worker per CPU**.",
      "source_hash": 8153378064814311622,
      "context_hash": 3041124292582506934,
      "translation": "핵심 특성: **커널은 CPU마다 실행 가능한 worker를 정확히 하나씩 유지하려고 합니다**.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "CPU": "CPU",
        "kernel": "커널"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:00:43.812224Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:7/block:2/seg:1",
      "source": "If a worker sleeps (waiting on I/O or a mutex), the kernel may create another worker to keep the CPU busy.",
      "source_hash": 9805248641492560267,
      "context_hash": 14674841697450712939,
      "translation": "worker가 (I/O나 뮤텍스를 기다리며) 잠들면, 커널은 CPU를 계속 바쁘게 유지하기 위해 다른 worker를 생성할 수 있습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "CPU": "CPU",
        "kernel": "커널",
        "mutex": "뮤텍스"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:00:43.812225Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:7/block:4/seg:0",
      "source": "This avoids both CPU underutilization (when workers sleep) and thread explosion (cmwq reuses workers intelligently).",
      "source_hash": 8384570790641442362,
      "context_hash": 12522206742684725475,
      "translation": "이를 통해 (worker가 잠들 때의) CPU 활용률 저하와 (cmwq가 worker를 지능적으로 재사용하므로) 스레드 폭증을 모두 피할 수 있습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "CPU": "CPU"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:00:43.812225Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:8/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "flush_work vs cancel_work",
      "source_hash": 6374723008808251202,
      "context_hash": 2454188997657289475,
      "translation": "flush_work 대 cancel_work",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:00:43.812226Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:8/block:2/seg:0",
      "source": "Always use `cancel_*_sync()` in driver teardown to prevent use-after-free:",
      "source_hash": 13629955731008193780,
      "context_hash": 6222140580133782125,
      "translation": "use-after-free를 방지하려면 드라이버 해제(teardown) 과정에서 항상 `cancel_*_sync()`를 사용하십시오:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "driver": "드라이버",
        "use-after-free": "use-after-free"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:00:43.812226Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
